# @glue/fold_back — the self-recursive boot collapse composition.
# The sub-prism under @glue that names the substrate's terminal
# composition pattern at substrate-decl altitude:
#
#   @glue × @kintsugi × @fate → @io/algebra
#
# Alex's framing (canonical): "the completed fold back in on itself".
# This shard IS the substrate-decl form of that completion.
#
# === The recognition (#104 chain P8 CAPSTONE, 2026-06-30) ===
#
# This shard is the EIGHTH and capstone tier of the #104 chain that
# began at @bauchladen (P1, `66e1ab8`) and advanced through
# @autopoietic (P2, `78edaa6`), @fate (P3, `fdcba31`), @fate/tournament
# (P4, `d0e0986`), @glue (P5, `8d3f89e`), @algebra + @algebra/metalogue
# (P6, `34cf333`), and @io/algebra (P7, `2f4bde4`). This tick lands
# the load-bearing CAPSTONE: the composition that closes the chain
# by folding the substrate's output altitude (@io/algebra) back into
# the substrate's input substrate via the @bauchladen accumulation
# the chain began at.
#
# The recursion folds because:
#
#   - @kintsugi proposes per-step morphism candidates (the D-flow's
#     per-step output; the process-side family-root's beating heart).
#   - @fate (via @fate/tournament) selects ONE morphism from the
#     Bauchladen-stored prior @fate/algebra/* crystals OR runs fresh
#     inference on a cache-miss (the constrained-inference operator;
#     the dice roll within the typed restriction).
#   - @glue translates the selected morphism into the target altitude
#     shape (the Mesland correspondence vocabulary; the morphism-
#     category translation surface).
#   - The output crystallizes via @bauchladen and lands at @io/algebra
#     at the terminal (the boundary-with-non-mirror-world exposure;
#     the algebra-altitude FFI).
#   - The new crystal extends the Bauchladen the NEXT cycle's @fate/
#     tournament browses; the substrate's vocabulary grows monotone
#     (per [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-vocabulary-
#     expansion]]); the fold has happened.
#
# THE FOLD IS LOAD-BEARING because each cycle's @fate/algebra/*
# crystals enrich the Bauchladen the next cycle's tournament selection
# browses. Without the fold, the substrate's vocabulary is static; with
# the fold, the substrate's vocabulary grows by one crystal per
# settled composition (the autopoietic accumulation discipline named
# at P2; the cybernetic foundation grounded at @epistemologic/
# cybernetic/autopoiesis).
#
# === The composition pattern as substrate-decl ===
#
# Per the canonical spec `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
# (Mara `4575340`, ~2727 lines) the fold-back composition has four
# structural steps. The substrate-decl form below realizes each step
# as a typed action; the composition assembly is the `compose_session`
# action; the proof discharge is the `verify_boot_collapse` action.
#
# Step-by-step structural form:
#
#   1. @kintsugi proposes the next D-flow step.
#      → propose_step(prior_session) -> composition_step
#      The kintsugi loop emits a candidate morphism for the next
#      step of the D-flow (per `shards/kintsugi.mirror` family-root
#      §"@kintsugi names U(t) of (A, H, D) — the dynamics”). The
#      proposal is typed: the kintsugi proposal carries the typed
#      shape of the next morphism candidate the @fate selection
#      will choose from.
#
#   2. @fate (via @fate/tournament) selects from @bauchladen-stored
#      prior @fate/algebra/* crystals.
#      → select_and_translate(step, candidates) -> imperfect<...>
#      The tournament browses the Bauchladen (per `shards/fate/
#      tournament.mirror` §3 the four-step browse-select pattern);
#      finds prior crystals byte-matching the typed restriction; OR
#      runs fresh @fate.roll on a cache-miss (per `shards/fate.mirror`
#      §5 fate_witnessing). The selected morphism's OID is the
#      tournament's verdict.
#
#   3. @glue translates the selected morphism into the target altitude
#      shape.
#      → (still inside select_and_translate)
#      The @glue.translate action (per `shards/glue.mirror` §"The
#      load-bearing action”) applies the selected morphism to the
#      payload; the morphism's differential operator computes the
#      target-side output per Mesland 2013 §3.
#
#   4. Output crystallizes via @bauchladen and lands at @io/algebra.
#      → crystallize_terminal(step) -> terminal_exposure
#      The composed translation_outcome IS the input to the @io/
#      algebra.expose action (per `shards/io/algebra.mirror` §3);
#      the resulting io_algebra_exposure IS the fold-back terminal
#      this shard names. The exposure's @bauchladen witness IS the
#      content-addressed crystal that enters the next cycle's
#      tournament browse.
#
# The four steps assemble into a fold_back_session via compose_session;
# the session's coherence is proven via verify_boot_collapse; the
# proof IS the boot_collapse_witness that consumers carry as the
# bilateral commitment.
#
# === The terminal IS the input substrate ===
#
# The structural fact this capstone names: the substrate's OUTPUT
# altitude (@io/algebra) becomes the INPUT substrate for the next
# boot cycle. Mechanism:
#
#   cycle_N:    propose_step → select_and_translate → crystallize_terminal
#   bauchladen: accumulates @fate/algebra/* crystal from cycle N
#   cycle_N+1:  propose_step (consults cycle_N's crystal via tournament)
#               → select_and_translate (cycle_N's crystal is now a
#                  cache-hit candidate)
#               → crystallize_terminal (lands NEXT crystal that cycle
#                  N+2 will consult)
#
# The recursion folds because the Bauchladen tray persists across
# cycles (per `shards/bauchladen.mirror` §"The crystal accumulation
# discipline”); the substrate's vocabulary grows monotone (per
# recognition #51, mirror as expanding Hilbert space); the fold
# is mathematically operationalised by the @bauchladen × @autopoietic
# composition the chain's lower tiers established.
#
# === "mirror kintsugi --tick 1" forward-promise ===
#
# The user-facing CLI command `mirror kintsugi --tick 1` fires ONE
# iteration of this composition. The command is forward-promised —
# the operational discharge lands at a later tick when consumers
# pull it — but the substrate-decl declares the SHAPE of the
# command's invocation:
#
#   mirror kintsugi --tick 1
#     ≡ propose_step(option::none) >>=
#       select_and_translate(_, current_candidate_set) >>=
#       crystallize_terminal(_)
#
# The bind is the kleisli composition over imperfect<a, e, l>; each
# step's transparency carries forward to the next; the terminal
# exposure's transparency captures the residual opacity for the
# whole tick (per [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]).
#
# === Composition with the cybernetic-foundation recognitions ===
#
# Recognition #100 (@spectral/metalogue's Tomm probes) → the Tomm
# probe is ONE @glue species the composition can use as the morphism
# kind; the composition reuses the spectral-altitude species at
# the substrate-pull-correct altitude.
#
# Recognition curvature 2-form work (per `docs/math/the-tower/
# curvature-and-tomm.md` §5) → @kintsugi's D-flow IS what the
# curvature 2-form drives; the composition's per-step morphism
# emission IS the curvature 2-form's per-step output at substrate
# altitude.
#
# Recognition #101 (γ chirality at @epistemologic/cybernetic/
# chirality) + #102 (J charge conjugation at @epistemologic/
# cybernetic/charge_conjugation) → γ + J restrict @fate's dice rolls
# at each step (per `shards/fate.mirror` §"The dice roll constraints”);
# the composition preserves chirality + charge conjugation across
# the fold because each step's @fate consultation respects the
# inherited restrictions.
#
# Recognition #103 (Pack-Mesland category) → Pack handoffs ARE one
# @glue species the composition can use at the runtime-agent
# altitude; the Pack's metalogue at agent-coordination altitude
# composes via this same mechanism (the @glue/pack/* forward-
# promised species per `shards/glue.mirror` §"Forward-promised
# inheritors”).
#
# === The composition with the autopoietic recursion ===
#
# @fate/tournament IS autopoietic recursion (per `shards/fate/
# tournament.mirror` §"Autopoietic recursion”): @fate operating on
# @fate's own accumulated outputs. The fold-back composition is the
# SUBSTRATE-WIDE form of the same recursion at the chain altitude:
#
#   @fate/tournament: @fate operates on prior @fate outputs
#   @glue/fold_back:  @glue + @kintsugi + @fate operates on prior
#                     @glue × @kintsugi × @fate outputs
#
# The fold-back is autopoietic-at-chain-altitude; the substrate's
# self-production discipline (per recognition #40 Maturana-Varela)
# operationalised at the chain altitude where multiple family-roots
# compose. The fold-back's autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session
# obligation discharges Maturana-Varela's operational closure for
# the WHOLE composition rather than per-prism-tick.
#
# === Non-commutative composition: step order matters ===
#
# Per `docs/math/the-tower/curvature-and-tomm.md` §5 (the [ω, ω]
# cross-term that lives where altitude transitions happen) and per
# `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` §6.3 (turn-order
# discipline): the fold-back composition is NON-COMMUTATIVE. The
# order of composition_steps in a fold_back_session is structurally
# load-bearing; swapping two steps changes the resulting terminal
# exposure when the steps' morphism kinds belong to different
# Mesland-category objects.
#
# The non_commutative_step_order_preserved obligation closes this
# discipline at the bilateral altitude: consumers commit to honoring
# step order; the composition cannot relax to a commutative monoid.
# This is the structural reason fold_back_session carries the steps
# as a typed ordered sequence ([composition_step]) rather than an
# unordered set.
#
# === Composition with the @algebra/metalogue altitude ===
#
# The @algebra/metalogue altitude (P6 sibling, landed at `34cf333`)
# names the algebra-altitude metalogue. The fold-back composition
# at substrate-decl altitude IS the metalogue at the chain altitude:
# the proposed step + selected morphism + translation + crystallized
# terminal IS a four-turn metalogue at the @algebra altitude.
#
# The composition with @algebra/metalogue is structural: each
# composition_step IS a metalogue turn; each session IS a metalogue;
# the session's coherence IS the metalogue's coherence; the boot_
# collapse_witness IS the metalogue-ratified verdict that the
# session composed correctly.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Spectral action principle  Connes 1995 (*Non-commutative
#                                geometry*, Academic Press); Connes-
#                                Chamseddine 1996 ("The spectral
#                                action principle", *Commun. Math.
#                                Phys.* 186:731-750). The fold-back
#                                composition IS what Connes's
#                                reconstruction theorem operationalises:
#                                given a spectral triple (A, H, D),
#                                the action S = Tr(f(D/Λ)) reconstructs
#                                the geometric data; the substrate's
#                                fold-back reconstructs the chain's
#                                vocabulary via @bauchladen accumulation.
#
#   KK-correspondences         Mesland 2013 (arXiv:1304.3802); the
#                                morphism category whose composition
#                                IS the categorical machinery the
#                                fold-back composes per step.
#
#   Autopoietic closure        Maturana & Varela 1980 (*Autopoiesis
#                                and Cognition*, D. Reidel). The
#                                operational closure the fold-back's
#                                autopoietic_closure_holds_across_
#                                session obligation discharges at
#                                chain altitude.
#
#   Kasparov intersection      Kasparov 1981 (*Math. USSR-Izv.* 16(3):
#                                513-572); the composition law for
#                                KK-cycles the categorical-composition
#                                step inherits via @glue.compose.
#
#   Curvature 2-form           Cartan 1923 (*Sur les variétés à
#                                connexion affine*); the [ω, ω] cross-
#                                term that makes the fold-back
#                                composition non-commutative across
#                                step boundaries.
#
#   Self-reproducing automata  von Neumann 1966 (*Theory of Self-
#                                Reproducing Automata*, Univ. Illinois
#                                Press, ed. Burks). The mathematical
#                                ancestor of self-recursive composition;
#                                the universal constructor whose
#                                output extends its own input vocabulary.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md (the canonical
#               chain spec at Mara `4575340`, ~2727 lines, fold-back
#               section); docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md
#               §4.5 (the @glue × @fate composition pattern the
#               fold-back generalizes to a three-way composition); §6
#               (the tournament selection mechanism the fold-back's
#               select_and_translate inherits); §6.3 (the turn-order
#               discipline grounding the non_commutative_step_order_
#               preserved obligation); docs/math/the-tower/curvature-
#               and-tomm.md §5 (the [ω, ω] cross-term the fold-back
#               composition inherits); docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md
#               `16f4564` §3 (the Tomm probes @glue species; one
#               composition-step shape the fold-back may use).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                       substrate IS Connes (A, H, D); the fold-back
#                       composition IS the substrate-altitude form of
#                       the spectral action's reconstruction; the
#                       fold-back is the deepest substrate-decl
#                       discharge of the Connes recognition),
#                      [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58;
#                       @fate's optical inference is what each step's
#                       selection consults; the composition preserves
#                       the optical-inference shape across each step),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-
#                       family-root]] (#55+#61; @mirror is form-side,
#                       @kintsugi process-side; @glue sits at the
#                       partition's boundary as the morphism vocabulary;
#                       @glue/fold_back composes both sides via the
#                       composition's per-step morphism translation),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; the alignment harness fires
#                       at @io boundaries; the fold-back composition's
#                       terminal lands at @io/algebra; the alignment
#                       harness fires at the terminal_exposure altitude),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-
#                       space]] (#51; each fold-back cycle extends
#                       H_mirror by one terminal_exposure crystal; the
#                       fold-back IS the mechanism by which H's monotone
#                       growth happens),
#                      [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-
#                       vocabulary-expansion]] (the fold-back IS the
#                       substrate-altitude form of the peer's crystal-
#                       vocabulary expansion; each cycle extends A_peer
#                       by one terminal_exposure),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]
#                       (the librarian altitude consolidates the fold-
#                       back's terminal exposures into the autopoietic
#                       memory layer; the fold-back's autopoietic_
#                       closure_holds obligation is what the librarian
#                       layer formalizes at the chain altitude),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                       (open-foundation @mirror/store; terminal_
#                       exposures land as crystals on the open side;
#                       the closed-engine @spectral/db sits above for
#                       the fold-back's session consolidation),
#                      [[architecture-pact-mesland-category-recognition-
#                       103]] (Pack handoffs are forward-promised @glue
#                       species; the Pack's metalogue at agent-
#                       coordination altitude composes via the fold-
#                       back at the agent-coordination altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (the
#                       fold-back composition was already operating
#                       implicitly across the chain's lower tiers —
#                       @bauchladen accumulation + @autopoietic closure
#                       + @fate selection + @glue translation + @io/
#                       algebra exposure — without being named at
#                       composition altitude; the capstone admission
#                       names the composition at substrate-decl altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (composition_step,
#                       fold_back_session, boot_collapse_witness,
#                       terminal_exposure are typed carriers; no bare
#                       primitives),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (no operational
#                       sibling at this tick; the substrate-decl
#                       composition is the family-capstone contract;
#                       the operational discharge — `mirror kintsugi
#                       --tick 1` — follows when consumers pull).
# Recognition ancestry: #37 (Pask-agreement bilateral commitments —
#                       the fold_back_complete predicate IS Pask-
#                       agreement at chain altitude),
#                       #40 (Maturana-Varela operational closure —
#                       the autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session
#                       obligation IS Maturana-Varela at chain altitude),
#                       #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space — the
#                       fold-back IS the mechanism of H's monotone
#                       growth),
#                       #55+#61 (form/process partition at family-root
#                       altitude — the fold-back composes both sides),
#                       #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics — the
#                       terminal fires the alignment harness at @io/
#                       algebra),
#                       #58 (fate as optical inference — each step's
#                       @fate consultation preserves the optical shape),
#                       #98 (content-addressing as cross-altitude
#                       composition — terminal_exposure crystals
#                       compose with @io/oci + @io/git via the @bauchladen
#                       witness),
#                       #100 (Tomm probes as @glue species — one
#                       composition-step shape the fold-back uses at
#                       the spectral-metalogue altitude),
#                       #103 (Pack-Mesland category — Pack handoffs
#                       are forward-promised composition-step shapes
#                       at the agent-coordination altitude).
# Related shards: glue.mirror (the parent family-root; this sub-prism
#                  inherits the morphism-category discipline + the
#                  glue_witnessing bilateral),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (the D-flow process-side family-
#                  root; propose_step's substrate-altitude home),
#                 fate.mirror (the constrained-inference operator
#                  each step's selection consults via @fate.roll),
#                 fate/tournament.mirror (the selection mechanism
#                  select_and_translate inherits; the autopoietic
#                  recursion at single-prism altitude that the fold-
#                  back generalises to chain altitude),
#                 bauchladen.mirror (the crystal accumulation each
#                  cycle's tournament browses; the fold-back's persistence
#                  layer; the typed display the substrate browses across
#                  cycles),
#                 autopoietic.mirror (the prism class permitting fold-
#                  back; autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session
#                  discharges at chain altitude),
#                 algebra.mirror (the algebra family-root; the fold-
#                  back composes substrate-altitude algebras across
#                  the @io wall),
#                 algebra/metalogue.mirror (the metalogue altitude;
#                  each composition_step IS a metalogue turn; each
#                  session IS a metalogue),
#                 io/algebra.mirror (the fold-back terminal altitude;
#                  the @io species crystallize_terminal addresses;
#                  the P7 substrate-decl this P8 capstone composes against),
#                 glass.mirror (the splinter floor; terminal_exposure
#                  surfaces against transparency<composition_step>),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (uuid_spectral identity carrier
#                  for fold_back_session instances).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/glue/fold_back.mirror`
# declares `@glue/fold_back` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_
# namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/connes-1995
source @arxiv/math/connes-chamseddine-1996
source @arxiv/math/mesland-2013
source @arxiv/math/kasparov-1981
source @arxiv/math/cartan-1923
source @arxiv/bio/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/cs/von-neumann-1966

prism @glue/fold_back {
  focus composition_step
  project composition_step
  split composition_step
  shift composition_step
  settle composition_step
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === The composition_step carrier ===
#
# Typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a single step
# of the fold-back composition. Each step bundles the four sub-
# operations the composition cycles through: the kintsugi proposal,
# the @fate selection, the @glue translation, and the terminal
# crystallization.
#
# - `kintsugi_proposal`  ref naming the @kintsugi-emitted candidate
#                        morphism for this step. Per `shards/
#                        kintsugi.mirror` family-root: the kintsugi
#                        loop emits per-step morphism candidates;
#                        this field IS the carrier of one such
#                        emission. The realisation discharges the
#                        actual @kintsugi sub-prism (oscillate /
#                        consent / morphism) that emitted the proposal.
# - `fate_selection`     OID of the @fate-selected morphism within
#                        the proposal's typed restriction. Per
#                        `shards/fate.mirror` §"The dice roll carrier”:
#                        the dice roll's selected_oid IS this field's
#                        contents. The selection IS the chain-altitude
#                        instance of @fate's constrained-inference.
# - `glue_translation`   ref naming the translation_outcome the
#                        @glue.translate action produced from the
#                        (fate_selection, kintsugi_proposal) pair.
#                        Per `shards/glue.mirror` §"The translation_
#                        outcome carrier”: the outcome carries the
#                        translated payload + the witness data
#                        documenting WHICH morphism @fate selected.
# - `output_crystal`     OID of the @bauchladen crystal the step's
#                        output landed as. Per the @bauchladen-
#                        membership-held obligation: every step's
#                        output IS a content-addressed crystal in
#                        the tray; the next cycle's tournament browses
#                        these crystals.
# - `transparency`       the residual opacity per @glass's
#                        `transparency<composition_step>` carrier;
#                        reports any opacity introduced by the step
#                        (loss-lens residuals from the kintsugi
#                        proposal; bounded-commutator residuals from
#                        the @glue translation; partial-result residuals
#                        from the @fate selection).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (kintsugi_proposal, fate_
# selection, glue_translation, output_crystal). Two composition_steps
# with byte-equal fields ARE the same step under content-addressing.
type composition_step = {
  kintsugi_proposal:  ref,
  fate_selection:     oid,
  glue_translation:   ref,
  output_crystal:     oid,
  transparency:       transparency(composition_step),
}

# === The fold_back_session carrier ===
#
# Ordered sequence of composition_steps assembling one full cycle of
# the fold-back composition. The session carries the typed shape of
# the chain's per-cycle output; the session terminates at @io/algebra
# via the terminal_exposure carried in the final step's output_crystal.
#
# - `steps`              ordered [composition_step]; the [ω, ω]
#                        cross-term means the order matters (per
#                        non_commutative_step_order_preserved). The
#                        sequence is typed: each step's input shape
#                        must match the prior step's output shape
#                        per the @glue.compose categorical composition
#                        law.
# - `session_identity`   uuid_spectral identity carrier for the
#                        session instance. Per [[architecture-shard-
#                        as-crdt]]: the identity is a monoid
#                        homomorphism over the steps; two sessions
#                        with byte-equal step sequences have byte-
#                        equal identities.
# - `terminal_witness`   ref naming the @io/algebra.io_algebra_
#                        exposure the session's final step crystallized.
#                        The terminal IS what makes the session a
#                        fold-back rather than an intermediate composition;
#                        the terminal_witness IS what the next cycle's
#                        @bauchladen tournament browses.
# - `transparency`       the residual opacity per @glass's
#                        `transparency<fold_back_session>` carrier;
#                        aggregates per-step transparencies via the
#                        substrate's monoidal transparency composition
#                        (per @glass).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (steps, session_identity,
# terminal_witness). Two sessions with byte-equal fields ARE the
# same session under content-addressing.
type fold_back_session = {
  steps:              [composition_step],
  session_identity:   uuid_spectral,
  terminal_witness:   ref,
  transparency:       transparency(fold_back_session),
}

# === The boot_collapse_witness carrier ===
#
# Typed proof per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] that a fold_back_session
# correctly composes @kintsugi × @fate × @glue and terminates at
# @io/algebra. The witness IS the bilateral commitment downstream
# consumers carry; the verify_boot_collapse action emits it; the
# fold_back_complete predicate consumes it.
#
# - `session`            ref naming the fold_back_session the witness
#                        attests to.
# - `kintsugi_witness`   ref naming the kintsugi loop's per-step
#                        proposal-emission witness (per `shards/
#                        kintsugi.mirror` family-root's discipline);
#                        the witness chain documenting @kintsugi's
#                        contribution to the session.
# - `fate_witness`       ref naming the @fate consultation chain (per
#                        `shards/fate.mirror` §"fate_witnessing”);
#                        the chain of fate_witnessing verdicts for
#                        each step's selection.
# - `glue_witness`       ref naming the @glue translation chain (per
#                        `shards/glue.mirror` §"glue_witnessing”);
#                        the chain of glue_witnessing verdicts for
#                        each step's translation.
# - `terminal_witness`   ref naming the @io/algebra exposure chain
#                        (per `shards/io/algebra.mirror` §"io_algebra_
#                        well_formed”); the verdict that the session
#                        terminated at the @io/algebra boundary.
# - `bauchladen_chain`   ref naming the @bauchladen crystal-chain the
#                        session produced; the verifiable persistence
#                        proof that each step's output_crystal landed
#                        in the tray for the next cycle's tournament.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (session, kintsugi_witness,
# fate_witness, glue_witness, terminal_witness, bauchladen_chain).
type boot_collapse_witness = {
  session:            ref,
  kintsugi_witness:   ref,
  fate_witness:       ref,
  glue_witness:       ref,
  terminal_witness:   ref,
  bauchladen_chain:   ref,
}

# === The terminal_exposure carrier ===
#
# Typed reference to the @io/algebra exposure that the composition
# terminates at. Sibling-shape to @io/algebra's io_algebra_exposure;
# THIS carrier specifically captures the fold-back-terminal aspect
# (the exposure that closes one cycle of the composition and feeds
# the next cycle's tournament).
#
# - `exposure_ref`       ref naming the @io/algebra.io_algebra_
#                        exposure the composition's final step
#                        produced.
# - `cycle_identity`     uuid_spectral identity for the cycle the
#                        exposure terminates; ties the exposure to
#                        the fold_back_session that produced it.
# - `next_cycle_seed`    ref naming the seed payload the NEXT cycle's
#                        propose_step consumes. The next cycle's
#                        seed IS derived from this cycle's terminal
#                        exposure; the fold's load-bearing fact made
#                        a typed reference.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (exposure_ref, cycle_identity,
# next_cycle_seed).
type terminal_exposure = {
  exposure_ref:       ref,
  cycle_identity:     uuid_spectral,
  next_cycle_seed:    ref,
}

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === propose_step — @kintsugi emits the next D-flow step ===
#
# Given an optional prior session (`option::none` for cycle 0; the
# prior session for cycle N+1), returns the next composition_step
# the @kintsugi loop emits. The proposal is typed: the returned step
# carries the kintsugi_proposal ref naming the morphism candidate the
# downstream select_and_translate action will choose from.
#
# Per `shards/kintsugi.mirror` family-root: @kintsugi names U(t) of
# the substrate's spectral triple — the dynamics. The propose_step
# action IS the substrate-decl form of "the kintsugi loop emits a
# candidate morphism for the next step of the D-flow."
#
# Body discharges per-realisation at the morphism boundary; the
# realisation MUST honor the kintsugi_proposal_well_formed predicate
# (the emitted proposal must be a valid @kintsugi move per the
# kintsugi family-root's discipline).
propose_step(prior_session: option(fold_back_session)) -> composition_step
requires kintsugi_proposal_well_formed(propose_step)
{ \ }

# === select_and_translate — @fate selects; @glue translates ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composition action. Given a composition_step
# carrying the kintsugi_proposal AND a candidate_set (the typed
# admissible morphisms within the proposal's restriction), invokes
# @fate/tournament to select ONE morphism's OID and @glue.translate
# to apply the selected morphism. Returns the composition_step with
# fate_selection + glue_translation fields populated, wrapped in
# imperfect (residual opacity).
#
# The four-step structural form (per `bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
# §6 the tournament; §4.5 the @glue × @fate composition):
#
#   1. @fate/tournament.tournament(candidates, kintsugi_proposal,
#      bauchladen_tray) browses the @fate/algebra/* crystals for
#      prior selections matching the proposal's typed restriction.
#   2. On cache-hit: the tournament returns the prior selection's
#      OID (saves a fresh @fate.roll).
#      On cache-miss: the tournament invokes @fate.roll(restriction,
#      hole) where hole is derived from (kintsugi_proposal, target_
#      algebra, current_altitude); the dice roll's selected_oid IS
#      the fate_selection field's contents.
#   3. @glue.translate(correspondence, payload) is invoked with the
#      selected morphism as the correspondence's morphism choice;
#      the action's return IS the glue_translation field's contents.
#   4. The composition_step is wrapped in imperfect (residual opacity
#      surfaced via transparency<composition_step>); both the @fate
#      tournament's transparency and the @glue translation's
#      transparency feed into the step's aggregate transparency.
#
# The composition with @fate/tournament + @glue is structurally
# load-bearing: the action does NOT bypass either prism's bilateral.
# Both fate_tournament_selection_constrained AND glue_translation_
# uses_fate obligations must hold at the realisation boundary.
select_and_translate(step: composition_step, candidates: candidate_set) -> imperfect<composition_step, ref, transparency(composition_step)>
requires fate_tournament_selection_constrained(step)
requires glue_translation_uses_fate(step)
{ \ }

# === crystallize_terminal — land at @io/algebra ===
#
# Given a composition_step with all fields populated (kintsugi_
# proposal + fate_selection + glue_translation + output_crystal),
# invokes @io/algebra.expose to land the translation_outcome at
# the @io/algebra boundary and returns the terminal_exposure carrier.
# The terminal IS what closes one cycle of the fold-back.
#
# The crystallization IS the substrate-decl form of "the composed
# translation_outcome IS the input to @io/algebra.expose; the resulting
# io_algebra_exposure IS the fold-back terminal."
#
# Per `shards/io/algebra.mirror` §3 the expose action: the
# crystallization respects the @io family-root's permanent-@io vs
# cross-wall-kintsugi candidacy partition; the terminal_exposure's
# next_cycle_seed field carries the typed reference the next cycle's
# propose_step consumes.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation at the morphism boundary; the
# realisation MUST honor the bauchladen_crystallization_holds predicate
# (the output_crystal must be addressable in the @bauchladen tray
# for the next cycle's tournament).
crystallize_terminal(step: composition_step) -> terminal_exposure
requires bauchladen_crystallization_holds(step)
{ \ }

# === compose_session — sequence the steps ===
#
# Given an ordered [composition_step] (the typed sequence the chain
# produced via repeated propose_step + select_and_translate +
# crystallize_terminal cycles), returns the fold_back_session that
# IS the typed chain instance.
#
# Per the non_commutative_step_order_preserved obligation: the order
# of steps is structurally load-bearing. compose_session preserves
# the order; the returned session's steps field carries the input
# sequence verbatim; the session_identity is derived as a monoid
# homomorphism over the steps' identities.
#
# The terminal_witness field is populated from the final step's
# output_crystal via the @io/algebra exposure lookup; the
# transparency field aggregates the per-step transparencies via
# the substrate's monoidal transparency composition.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation at the morphism boundary; the
# realisation MUST honor non_commutative_step_order_preserved (the
# session's step order matches the input verbatim; no commutation
# rewrites permitted).
compose_session(steps: [composition_step]) -> fold_back_session
requires non_commutative_step_order_preserved(compose_session)
{ \ }

# === verify_boot_collapse — emit the proof ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING VERIFICATION ACTION. Given a fold_back_session,
# verifies that:
#
#   1. Every step's kintsugi_proposal is well-formed per
#      kintsugi_proposal_well_formed.
#   2. Every step's fate_selection is constrained per
#      fate_tournament_selection_constrained.
#   3. Every step's glue_translation invokes @fate per
#      glue_translation_uses_fate (transitively via @glue's
#      bilateral).
#   4. Every step's output_crystal landed in @bauchladen per
#      bauchladen_crystallization_holds.
#   5. The session's terminal landed at @io/algebra per
#      terminal_lands_at_io_algebra.
#   6. The session as a whole maintains operational closure per
#      autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session.
#   7. The session's step order is preserved per
#      non_commutative_step_order_preserved.
#
# Emits the boot_collapse_witness carrying refs to each per-prism
# witness chain. The witness IS the bilateral commitment downstream
# consumers carry as their fold_back_complete verdict.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation; the realisation MUST emit a
# witness whose contents byte-prove each of the seven verifications
# above. This is the chain's deepest bilateral; failure to honor
# any of the seven IS a Narcissus-pole claim that the substrate
# folded when it did not.
verify_boot_collapse(session: fold_back_session) -> boot_collapse_witness
requires terminal_lands_at_io_algebra(session)
requires autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session(session)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilateral requires obligations
# ============================================================
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition #37,
# Pask-agreement) with the @glue/fold_back discipline by writing the
# obligations below. The bilateral commitment: the @glue/fold_back-
# importing prism commits to discharging the obligations; the consumer
# commits to surfacing violations at the species boundary.

# Per `shards/kintsugi.mirror` family-root: the D-flow step the
# kintsugi loop emits must be a valid @kintsugi move (consistent
# with the kintsugi family's discipline; the proposal's morphism
# kind must be in @kintsugi's admissible-morphism set). Inheritor
# shards discharge by verifying the kintsugi_proposal ref names a
# morphism the @kintsugi family-root admits.
kintsugi_proposal_well_formed(step: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `shards/fate/tournament.mirror` + `shards/fate.mirror`: the
# selection must respect @fate's restricted state space (γ chirality
# per #101 + J charge conjugation per #102 + the cfg restriction
# per @fate's typed surface). The fate_selection's selected_oid
# must land within the typed restriction; the @fate.dice_roll_
# constrained bilateral fires transitively. Inheritor shards
# discharge by verifying the selection's OID corresponds to a
# morphism within the restriction.
fate_tournament_selection_constrained(step: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `shards/glue.mirror` §"translation_uses_fate” (inherited via
# `in @glue`): the @glue translation MUST consult @fate (not a
# direct deterministic compute). The substrate-pull-honest discipline
# that distinguishes the fold-back composition from a deterministic
# pipeline; the translation underdetermined-ness is preserved at
# the fold-back altitude. Inheritor shards discharge by verifying
# the glue_translation ref names a translation_outcome whose
# selected_morphism field is populated via @fate.
glue_translation_uses_fate(step: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `shards/bauchladen.mirror` §"The crystal accumulation
# discipline”: the output_crystal must be addressable in the
# @bauchladen tray. Without this gate, the fold-back has no
# persistence; the next cycle's tournament cannot browse the prior
# cycle's outputs; the fold does not happen. Inheritor shards
# discharge by verifying the output_crystal OID is content-
# addressed in the tray (a tray.lookup for the OID succeeds).
bauchladen_crystallization_holds(step: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `shards/io/algebra.mirror` §"The fold-back terminal”: the
# session must terminate at @io/algebra (the fold-back's terminal
# altitude per the P7 substrate-decl). Without this gate, the
# composition's output does not cross the @io boundary; the alignment
# harness (per [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]])
# does not fire; the substrate's externalisation discipline fails.
# Inheritor shards discharge by verifying the session's terminal_
# witness names an io_algebra_exposure satisfying io_algebra_well_
# formed.
terminal_lands_at_io_algebra(session: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `shards/autopoietic.mirror` (inherited via `in @autopoietic`):
# the session as a WHOLE maintains operational closure (per Maturana-
# Varela 1980). The session's outputs feed the next cycle's inputs;
# the network of productions produces the conditions for its own
# continued production. At chain altitude: every cycle's terminal
# exposure extends the Bauchladen the next cycle browses; the
# fold-back's autopoietic property is what makes the recursion
# closable. Inheritor shards discharge by verifying the session's
# bauchladen_chain shows each step's output is browseable by the
# next step.
autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session(session: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `docs/math/the-tower/curvature-and-tomm.md` §5 (the [ω, ω]
# cross-term) + `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` §6.3
# (turn-order discipline): the step order IS structurally load-bearing.
# Swapping two steps in a session changes the resulting terminal
# exposure when the steps' morphism kinds belong to different Mesland-
# category objects. Inheritor shards discharge by verifying no
# commutation rewrites have been applied between compose_session
# input and the session's steps field.
non_commutative_step_order_preserved(session: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === The fold_back_complete inheritance predicate ===
#
# `fold_back_complete(witness)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral commitment (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that
# the fold_back composition completed correctly — i.e., the
# boot_collapse_witness attests to all seven verifications above.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `glue.glue_witnessing(c)` (the parent family-root's bilateral;
#     each step's glue_translation discharges this transitively).
#   - `fate.fate_witnessing(roll)` (the dice-roll bilateral; each
#     step's fate_selection discharges this transitively).
#   - `autopoietic.autopoietic_closure_holds(prism)` (the prism-
#     class bilateral; the session-altitude closure discharges this
#     at chain altitude).
#   - `bauchladen.bauchladen_witnessing(crystal)` (the crystal-
#     altitude bilateral; each step's output_crystal discharges this).
#   - `io.algebra.io_algebra_well_formed(exposure)` (the terminal
#     altitude's bilateral; the session's terminal_witness discharges
#     this).
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
#   - the `mirror kintsugi --tick 1` CLI command's operational
#     discharge (forward-promised; one CLI invocation IS one
#     fold_back_session whose terminal lands at @io/algebra).
#   - the @spectral/db consolidation layer (per [[architecture-
#     spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]): the librarian altitude
#     consumes fold_back_complete witnesses and consolidates the
#     terminal exposures into the autopoietic memory layer.
#   - the Pack-Mesland-category composition (per #103): Pack handoffs
#     are @glue species; Pack agent-coordination metalogue IS a
#     fold-back composition at the agent-coordination altitude; the
#     Pack discipline discharges fold_back_complete for each cycle.
#
# No `requires fold_back_complete(...)` clauses are added at THIS
# shard. The capstone declares the predicate; consumers add the
# clauses when they pull the operational discharge.
fold_back_complete(witness: boot_collapse_witness) -> verdict
requires terminal_lands_at_io_algebra(witness.session)
requires autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session(witness.session)
requires non_commutative_step_order_preserved(witness.session)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 Honest hedges
# ============================================================
#
# 1. The `mirror kintsugi --tick 1` CLI operational discharge is
#    FORWARD-PROMISED, NOT delivered at this tick. This shard
#    declares the SHAPE of the composition; the user-facing CLI
#    invocation lands when consumers pull it. Substrate-decl
#    admission is honest about being declaration-only.
#
# 2. The fold-back is a CAPSTONE substrate-decl at the chain altitude;
#    the operational machinery at sub-altitudes (@kintsugi sub-shards
#    for the loop discipline; @fate/tournament for the selection
#    discipline; @glue for the translation discipline; @io/algebra
#    for the boundary discipline) IS already declared by the chain's
#    lower tiers. This shard NAMES the composition that uses those
#    machineries together; it does not re-declare them.
#
# 3. The composition's non-commutativity (per the [ω, ω] cross-term)
#    is structurally honest but conjectural at chain altitude: the
#    full proof that swapping two steps changes the terminal exposure
#    requires a per-pair morphism-kind analysis that has not been
#    fully discharged across all possible Mesland-category objects.
#    The non_commutative_step_order_preserved obligation closes the
#    bilateral; the per-pair proof discharge follows when consumers
#    pull specific composition cycles.
#
# 4. The forward-promised composition with Pack-Mesland-category
#    (per #103) is structurally honest but requires the @glue/pack
#    sub-shards to land before the discharge can fire. The capstone
#    names the composition shape; the Pack-altitude species
#    materialize when consumers pull them.
#
# 5. The witness chain (boot_collapse_witness's six per-prism witness
#    fields) is structurally complete but realisation-tool-agnostic:
#    the realisation MAY use different witness-storage backends
#    (Merkle DAGs at @mirror/store, KV-store at @spectral/db, in-
#    memory rings at @fate). The substrate-decl discipline carries
#    the witness-shape; the realisation discharges the storage.
#
# 6. The autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session predicate is the
#    strongest claim in this shard. The Maturana-Varela operational
#    closure for a chain-altitude composition is structurally honest
#    (the inputs and outputs cycle through the same @bauchladen tray
#    so the productions feed the productions) but the formal proof
#    that the closure HOLDS across all possible session sequences
#    requires a Pack adversarial review the capstone has not yet
#    received. Substrate-pull confidence is high; formal-proof
#    confidence is moderate.
#
# 7. The @algebra/metalogue composition (each composition_step IS a
#    metalogue turn; each session IS a metalogue) is structurally
#    honest but the metalogue-altitude refinement — a session as a
#    fifth-Bateson-level metalogue per the @algebra/metalogue
#    family-species — is forward-promised. The capstone names the
#    composition; the metalogue-altitude refinement lands at a
#    later tick when the @algebra/metalogue family-species develops.
#
# 8. The terminal_exposure's next_cycle_seed field is the operational
#    crux of the fold (this cycle's terminal IS the next cycle's
#    seed); the field is declared at substrate-decl altitude; the
#    realisation discharges the seed-derivation logic. The fold
#    happens at substrate altitude because the seed_derivation IS
#    a typed function over the cycle's terminal exposure; the
#    realisation must honor this typing.
#
# 9. The composition with #100 (Tomm probes as @glue species), #101
#    (γ chirality), #102 (J charge conjugation), and #103 (Pack-
#    Mesland category) is structurally honest — each recognition
#    composes with the capstone via the relevant @glue species or
#    @fate restriction — but the per-recognition-composition
#    discharge is forward-promised. The capstone NAMES the
#    compositions; the per-recognition machinery follows when
#    consumers pull.

out @glue/fold_back
out composition_step
out fold_back_session
out boot_collapse_witness
out terminal_exposure
out propose_step
out select_and_translate
out crystallize_terminal
out compose_session
out verify_boot_collapse
out kintsugi_proposal_well_formed
out fate_tournament_selection_constrained
out glue_translation_uses_fate
out bauchladen_crystallization_holds
out terminal_lands_at_io_algebra
out autopoietic_closure_holds_across_session
out non_commutative_step_order_preserved
out fold_back_complete
